<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[Dear <span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);">[Insert Name]</span>,]]></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" height="300" >
<td tEditID="c1r2" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r2" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;">I would like to share some
information with you about type O blood and the impact your upcoming blood
drive can make. While all blood types are needed; blood types O negative and O
positive must be collected at a higher rate to keep up with hospital demand. </span><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;
color:#333333;background:white">In emergency situations when there’s no time to
determine a patient’s blood type, doctors reach for type O blood. These
critical blood types are always in high demand but often in low supply. It’s
important for you to know that the recruitment actions you take as a blood
program leader can directly impact our ability to respond to hospital demand. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"><br></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><u><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;">Next
Steps, immediately review the attached items: <o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p>

<ul style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-top: 0in;" type="disc">
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;">Info
     piece -</span></b><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;">
     what you should know before your drive and easy ways to increase your
     impact. <o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;">Donor
     email - </span></b><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;">a
     template you can customize and use to recruit eligible type O blood
     donors.</span></li></ul>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><u><span style="font-family:&quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;">Additional
tips for success:<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p>

<ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc">
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; margin-top: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;;">Before the blood drive, make a personal call to
     type O donors, reminding them why their appointment is needed and thank
     them for scheduling an appointment to give blood. </span><span style="font-family: &quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; margin-top: 0in; line-height: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;;">If a Power Red device is assigned to the blood
     drive, ensure the type O donor is educated on the process and, if
     eligible, is encouraged to donate Power Red.&nbsp; </span><span style="color: rgb(237, 27, 46); font-family: &quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">Thank you again for your
commitment as a blood program leader.</span><span style="font-family: &quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp; </span><span style="font-family: &quot;Akzidenz-Grotesk Std Regular&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">I
am confident that with some additional efforts, you will increase your type O
donors. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to reach out – I’m
always here to help!</span></p>]]></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" height="50" >
<td tEditID="c1r3" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r3" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">All the best,</span></font><div><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);">[Insert Name]</span></div>]]></td>
